.TH SWAYDESK-THEME-APP 1 2026-11-14 "swaydesk 0.1.10" "Sway desktop components"
.SH NAME
swaydesk\-theme\-app \- Desktop Theme application
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swaydesk\-theme\-app
.SH DESCRIPTION
A window to choose the GTK theme family, light or dark, and the accent color among the Papirus colors. Choosing only changes the preview; Apply (or Enter) applies it through the same code as swaydesk\-theme, and the window stays open. Opening it again raises the open window. Its menu entry is org.swaydesktop.Theme.
.PP
The switch "Use the wallpaper's color", above the colors, is accent_auto (on by default): the accent follows the wallpaper, as swaydesk\-theme accent\-auto does, and the dot beside it shows the color it gives now (the default accent, #199ca8, for a wallpaper without color or one that does not open). With it on, the colors are dimmed; choosing one turns it off. Apply saves the switch with the theme.
.PP
The Icons list, below the style, has the icon themes that can be chosen, each with a strip of its own icons (Papirus is one entry that follows the style). Changing it applies only the icons with Apply; the Papirus folder color only exists with Papirus, and with other icons the color changes the accent only.
.PP
The Cursor size list, below the icons, has the sizes the cursor theme has. Choosing one applies it at once, without
Apply, as swaydesk\-theme cursor does: GTK 4 and Qt 6 apps follow at once, older ones when they open again.
.PP
The session runs it under the name sway\-theme\-app (a link in the package's helper directory to /usr/bin/swaydesk\-theme\-app); the process name is sway\-theme\-app too.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Exit 0 at once without doing anything: the Python launchers use it to check that the binary and its libraries load.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/swaydesk/config.toml
The desktop configuration: language, accent color and accent_auto, GTK and icon themes, folder color, cursor size, file manager, weather location and holidays.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR swaydesk (7),
.BR swaydesk\-theme (1)
